Z||000000||Homicidal||06-19-2000||03:53 AM||||I am building the sub-box SOON.  But in my front trunk I have plastic "shelf" underneath the silver canister a/c thing, it runs along that the entire side of my trunk.  Do I need to cut that section off or cut into it at all for the box?||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||06-19-2000||07:31 AM||||AAaRRRGH!!!! Don't do it!! <BR>Now that I got yer attention, my advice to you would be to build your enclosure inside the car like I did. The sound quality is very good and you will not be broadcasting to thieves that you got funk in the trunk. Junkies won't hesitate ripping up a fiberglass hood if they think a high is underneath.<BR>If you do think that going in the trunk is best for ya, I would go to the local pick and pull and see if I could find an extra spare tire tub before hacking up the one in my car.<BR>Vaya con Dios, Homi.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||06-19-2000||11:08 AM||||Hehe, I already HAVE a 10" in my car!<P>This is my second sub, and from what Formula tells me, I don't have to cut anywhere.<P>But I'm curious if all Fieros have that extra "shelf" or not.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||06-19-2000||06:23 PM||||I dont know if there is a shelf in mine or not.  I didnt cut anything, I forget the dimensions of the box but if you take the botom measurement and measuer from the bottom corner(in the front trunk) there should be an inch or two of clearance.  If there is a shelf in there that is not in mine then there probably is a bolt holding it on someplace........<P>If the plastic your talking about is what the bootom of the tire sits on then your fine and dont need to cut anything.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BroCar 87||06-19-2000||07:56 PM||||Homicidal, I also have built a box in my front trunk. I have a 10 in the pass. seat floorboard and one in the front trunk now. Just did it this past Wednesday. I don't have a big amp on it yet but i can tell its there. I will try to put the dimentions on here if i can... give me sec. I hope this comes out. If it doesn't give me your e-mail and i will email you the real thing.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FrontCompartmentDimentions.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||BroCar 87||06-19-2000||08:00 PM||||OHHH also, NO you do not have to cut the lip under the A/C. Its there on all of them. My box IS removable. I have to put in the passenger side first when putting it back in but, THOSE are the dimentions I used. Sorry I don't have the angles of all the corners though. let me know if you need anything else too. I will check back up in here constantly tooo.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
